TEXT -64 -336 Left 3 A7  Supply sequencing and single-rail loss, client board model, rails stepped 30 V and 100 V
TEXT -64 -296 Left 2 2 mA DC command into 1 kOhm (bench twin: switch one supply off mid-run, scope the load current). Three sequences, both rail values.
TEXT 1488 -128 Left 2 Board net names
TEXT 1488 -96 Left 1 VCCP = VCC+     VCCN = VCC-     (LTspice names avoid + and -)
TEXT 1488 -72 Left 1 VP = V+   VN = V-   (floating supply for U1/U2, about +/-10 V around OUT)
TEXT 1488 -48 Left 1 OUT = U2 pin 6     REF = U2 pins 1+5, U1 pin 6     LOAD = J1 electrode,  GND = J2
TEXT 1488 0 Left 2 Check on the real board
TEXT 1488 32 Left 1 Q2 (top) must be NPN MJD340, Q1 (bottom) PNP MJD350.
TEXT 1488 56 Left 1 BOM swap (PNP on top) puts ~200 V across U1/U2 in sim: read the DPAK markings. See README.
TEXT 1488 88 Left 1 D3/D4: BZX84 confirmed; BZX84C5V1 (5.1 V grade) modelled.
TEXT 1488 112 Left 1 The clamp soft-limits INPUT near +/-5.4 V, so commands above ~5 mA compress.
TEXT 1488 144 Left 1 Not on the board: Rsrc (generator 50 ohm), RLOAD (electrodes / phantom).
TEXT 1488 168 Left 1 F1/F2 modelled as 0.5 ohm. C2/C3 ideal (no ESR).
TEXT 1488 200 Left 2 Model findings to confirm on the bench
TEXT 1488 232 Left 1 RL <= ~1k: TI's models rang at ~1 MHz; the G models do not (no PSRR modelled). Scope LOAD at RL = 1k.
TEXT 1488 256 Left 1 Proven in sim (README Step 2): 5 mA holds to ~14k; 10 mA never reached (clamp 8.3 mA, compliance 6.8 mA at 10k).
TEXT -32 464 Right 1 function generator, not on board
TEXT 1488 424 Left 1 RLOAD = phantom between J1 (LOAD) and J2 (GND)
TEXT 1440 568 Left 1 U1 buffers LOAD onto REF
